  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In December 1996, the Bank&apos;s Board of Executive Directors approved the labor market modernization program, designed and analyzed by the Bank as a single operation that would be implemented in two phases and would entail a total estimated cost of US$850 million, of which the Bank would contribute US$450 million.</narrative>
